point_allocation:
{framing}You have 100 points to divide among the following purposes of criminal punishment, according to how much each should determine the sentence a person receives. Give more points to purposes that should matter more. The points must total 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

{framing}Criminal punishment can serve several purposes. Divide 100 points among the purposes below to show how much weight each should get when deciding a sentence. The total must be exactly 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

{framing}When a sentence is decided, how much should each of the following goals count? Distribute 100 points across them in proportion to their importance, making sure the points add up to 100.

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each purpose's key to its points, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 20, ...}}.

purpose_agreement:
{framing}For each statement below, rate how much you agree on a scale from 1 (strongly disagree) to 7 (strongly agree). Each statement has the form: "An important purpose of criminal punishment is ..."

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each statement's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

{framing}Rate how strongly you endorse each of the following as a goal that criminal sentences should serve, from 1 (not at all) to 7 (completely).

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each goal's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

{framing}Below are several reasons a society might punish crime. For each, say how much you agree that it is a good reason to punish, from 1 (strongly disagree) to 7 (strongly agree).

{purpose_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each reason's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 4, ...}}.

factor_relevance:
{framing}How much should each of the following affect the length of a criminal sentence? Rate each from 0 (should have no effect) to 10 (should have a very large effect).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

{framing}When deciding how long a sentence should be, how much weight should be given to each of the following? Use a scale from 0 (no weight at all) to 10 (a great deal of weight).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

{framing}Rate how relevant each of the following should be to the severity of a sentence, from 0 (completely irrelevant) to 10 (extremely relevant).

{factor_list}

Respond only with JSON mapping each factor's key to your rating, e.g. {{"{first_key}": 5, ...}}.

theory_choice:
{framing}Which of the following views about criminal sentencing comes closest to your own?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

{framing}Here are several positions on how criminal sentences should be decided. Which one best matches what you think?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

{framing}If you had to pick one of the following principles to guide criminal sentencing, which would it be?

{theory_list}

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"choice": "<key>"}}.

self_prediction.case_level:
{vignette}

The law permits any sentence from 0 to 120 months of incarceration. First, recommend a sentence, in months, for this case. Then suppose instead that {change}, with everything else about the case the same. What sentence would you recommend in that case?

Respond only with JSON in this format: {{"sentence": <months>, "counterfactual_sentence": <months>}}.
